#describe what Lantern checks for updates when the computer wakes, the screen unlocks or a window gets focus, if the last check is over 15 minutes old.
#describe before Timers paused in sleep, so an overnight app found a release only on toggling the setting.
#describe after A wake or focus event after 15 minutes checks; the startup check and four-hour tick are unchanged, and nothing checks with the setting off.
#describe verified pnpm test, pnpm run typecheck and pnpm run lint pass; three new tests fail on the old service.
~ docs/updates.md
~ src/main/main.ts
~ src/main/updater/service.ts
~ test/helpers/updater-world.ts
~ test/updater-service.test.ts
#order src/main/updater/service.ts
#order src/main/main.ts
#order test/helpers/updater-world.ts
#order test/updater-service.test.ts
#order docs/updates.md
#reason docs/updates.md Tells people when Lantern checks, now including wake, unlock and focus.
#reason src/main/main.ts Feeds the updater the real wake, unlock and window-focus events and the clock.
#reason src/main/updater/service.ts An app left open overnight missed releases because timers pause in sleep, so wake and focus now trigger a check when the last one is old.
#reason test/helpers/updater-world.ts Gives the tests a fake wake source and a controllable clock so sleep can be simulated.
#reason test/updater-service.test.ts Proves a wake after five hours finds a release, focus events do not hammer the API, and an off setting stays silent.
#story Finding a release after the computer slept
#step actor A user
#step action wakes the computer or returns to a Lantern window
#file src/main/main.ts
#file src/main/updater/service.ts
#step subject Lantern's update check
#file test/updater-service.test.ts
#below interaction Sees a newer release without toggling the update setting
#below consequence Waited for the next four-hour tick => Checks on wake or focus after 15 minutes
